# GitNexus index — keep updated

The `.gitnexus/` code-intelligence index is **committed** to the repo. Agents use the **CLI** (`node .gitnexus/run.cjs`), not MCP.

## On start

Cloud Agent `start` runs `node scripts/gitnexus-sync.mjs startup`, which re-analyzes when needed and drops GitNexus's inner `.gitignore` so the index stays tracked.

If you are not on a Cloud Agent pod, run the same command once at the beginning of substantive work:

```bash
npm run gitnexus:startup
```

## Before finishing

Before your **final commit and push** for a task, refresh and stage the index:

```bash
npm run gitnexus:sync
```

This runs `node scripts/gitnexus-sync.mjs finish`, which re-analyzes, removes the inner `.gitignore`, and stages `.gitnexus/`, `AGENTS.md`, and `CLAUDE.md`. **Include those staged files in your commit** so the next agent starts with a current graph.

## Manual commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `node .gitnexus/run.cjs status` | Check freshness |
| `node .gitnexus/run.cjs analyze` | Rebuild index only |
| `npm run gitnexus:startup` | Start-of-work sync |
| `npm run gitnexus:sync` | End-of-work sync + stage |
